## 0. Document authority and use

This specification supplements, but does not replace, SRS 1.2. SRS defines business behavior; this file pins Android architecture, schema, state, protocol, and verification detail. The approved design reference explains rationale and operational trade-offs.

Implementation shall proceed feature by feature with tests first. No implementation agent may reinterpret a numeric threshold or security/business rule already fixed here. Backend-only features remain out of scope for Android 3.0.

The cleaned `feature/android-set-3.0-design` branch currently implements the Phase 1 encrypted platform foundation and a minimal launchable Compose shell. The target packages and behaviors in later sections remain scheduled work unless the roadmap records their completion. Android 2.1 periodic-email classes are deliberately excluded; later phases shall implement this specification directly and may reuse only isolated, verified techniques rather than copying the pilot architecture wholesale.

Production server, portal, AI, Vendor reconciliation, and GPS receiver implementations are outside this branch. The unchanged `main` branch remains the historical source/archive for server and receiver code.

